<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB details Philippine project.</title>
<headline>ABB details Philippine project.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss-Swedish engineering group ABB provided details for a contract already announced in Manila on Wednesday, saying the order was valued at nearly $90 million.</p>
<p>The project involves a contract to supply and construct two overhead 500-kilovolt power transmission lines in the Philippines on the main island of Luzon.</p>
<p>The contract was placed by National Power Corp (Napocor), the Philippine state-owned power utility. Napocor earlier said the order was valued at 2.282 billion pesos ($87 million).</p>
<p>ABB said the financing will be provided by the World Bank, adding construction is to begin by spring 1998.</p>
<p>The order was won by ABB unit  ABB SAE Sadelmi, Milan, Italy, which is already involved in two other power line projects for the same customer, ABB said.</p>
